      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is okay for now but eventually this should probably be refacored.. this class seems very susceptible to concurrency issues. ResponseRecord should either be internal state accessed by multiple threads through locked method calls on CapabilityRequestResponse (or a lock object) or a read-only final class that is created whenever getResponseRecord is called and all of this state is stored in CapabilityRequestResponse itself.\n\nIt is fine to use ResponseRecord as a data container, but it should not also be used as a data store without a copy mechanism",
